  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Infrastructure Regulatory Reform IDF Grant Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To develop the essential components of the new regulatory framework and to enhance the capacity of the State Energy Regulatory Commission (SERC) to perform regulatory tasks in the energy and water sectors. The key goal is to establish transparent rules and procedures guiding the operations of energy and water companies and to enhance the quality of SERC&apos;s regulatory decision-making in these sectors.  Achievement of this goal will benefit the consumerscomma improve conditions for operations and investment in energy and water infrastructure through greater transparency and predictability. Specificallycomma the grant will finance (a) development of methodologies for the setting of prices; (b) development of quality of service standards; and (c) training of regulatory staff. To develop the essential components of a new reagulatory framework for infrastructure services and to enhance the capacity of SEWRC to perform regulatory tasks.</narrative>
  </description>
